{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And Elohim said to Jacob, Return.</b> Scripture informs us that because of these three factors he fled without taking leave of Laban — unlike the custom of a man of his stature. For he reasoned that after Laban had accepted an evil report about him, if he knew of his departure he would rob him, as it says: <b>lest you rob my daughters</b>." "<b>And I will be with you.</b> So that no harm befall you on the journey."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {0 "The verse quoted, פן תגזל את בנותי, corresponds to Laban's words in Genesis 31:26; Sforno reads it as Jacob's own reasoning about what Laban would do."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:32:44.468179897Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}